Here’s the simplest **recursive C program** to print the **binary representation** of a number — clean, short, and to the point 👇  

```c
#include <stdio.h>

void printBinary(int n) {
    if (n > 1)
        printBinary(n / 2);   // Recursive call

    printf("%d", n % 2);      // Print the last bit
}

int main() {
    int num;
    printf("Enter a number: ");
    scanf("%d", &num);

    printf("Binary of %d is: ", num);
    printBinary(num);
    printf("\n");

    return 0;
}
```

### 🔍 Example:
**Input:** `13`  
**Output:** `Binary of 13 is: 1101`

